<h1>Project Report: D&amp;C MediaHouse Portfolio Website</h1><h2>1. Project Overview</h2><p><strong>Project Name:</strong> D&amp;C MediaHouse</p><p><strong>Live Site URL:</strong> <a href="https://www.dcmediahouse.in/">https://www.dcmediahouse.in/</a></p><p><strong>Description:</strong> A high-end cinematic portfolio website tailored for D&amp;C MediaHouse. The project focuses on delivering an immersive viewing experience, featuring adaptive video streaming (HLS) and modern, fluid animations to showcase media projects effectively.</p><h3>Author Details</h3><ul><li><strong>Name:</strong> Meet Sharma</li><li><strong>College / Institution:</strong> Raj Kumar Goel Institute Of Technology (Ghaziabad)</li><li><strong>Course:</strong> B.Tech CSE-DS Student (2023-2027)</li><li><strong>GitHub:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/LEGITKINGPIN">LEGITKINGPIN</a></li><li><strong>LinkedIn:</strong> <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/meet-sharma-m16042005">Meet Sharma</a></li></ul><h2>2. Technologies Used &amp; Architecture</h2><h3>Core Technologies</h3><ul><li><strong>Frontend Framework:</strong> Next.js 15 (App Router), React 19</li><li><strong>Styling:</strong> Tailwind CSS (v4)</li><li><strong>Content Management System (CMS):</strong> Sanity Studio (Headless CMS)</li><li><strong>Video Infrastructure &amp; Streaming:</strong> Mux (Adaptive HLS Streaming)</li><li><strong>Animations &amp; UI:</strong> Framer Motion (motion/react), Embla Carousel, Lucide React</li><li><strong>Languages:</strong> TypeScript, JavaScript</li><li><strong>DNS Management:</strong> Cloudflare (DNS-Only / Grey Cloud Mode)</li><li><strong>Deployment &amp; Hosting:</strong> Vercel</li></ul><p>The project follows a decoupled, headless architecture comprising a modern Next.js frontend and a Sanity-powered backend CMS.</p><h3>2.1. Frontend App (dc-mediahouse-next/ &amp; D&amp;C/)</h3><p>The frontend focuses on high performance and cinematic aesthetics. The project was originally built in Vite (React 19) and has since been migrated to Next.js for enhanced capabilities.</p><ul><li><strong>Framework:</strong> Next.js (App Router) migrating from Vite (React 19)</li><li><strong>Styling:</strong> Tailwind CSS (v4) with utility libraries like clsx and tailwind-merge for dynamic classes.</li><li><strong>Animations &amp; Transitions:</strong><ul><li>motion (Framer Motion) for sophisticated entry, exit, and scroll-driven animations.</li><li>embla-carousel-react for smooth, touch-friendly image/video galleries and carousels.</li></ul></li><li><strong>Media &amp; Video Streaming:</strong><ul><li>Adaptive HLS video streaming utilizing hls.js.</li><li>@mux/mux-player-react for highly optimized, cinematic video playback and integration with Mux video infrastructure.</li></ul></li><li><strong>CMS Integration:</strong> @sanity/client to fetch dynamic portfolio content from the backend studio.</li><li><strong>Fonts &amp; Optimization:</strong> next/font/google for optimized, layout-shift-free cinematic typography.</li><li><strong>UI Components:</strong> lucide-react for lightweight and scalable iconography.</li><li><strong>Deployment:</strong> Vercel / GitHub Actions for automated, zero-downtime deployments.</li><li><strong>DNS Infrastructure:</strong> Cloudflare manages the domain routing using a "DNS-Only" (Grey Cloud) setup. This directs traffic to Vercel's Edge Network without proxy interference, optimizing global resolution speed while retaining Vercel's native SSL provisioning and edge caching performance.</li></ul><h3>2.2. Backend CMS (studio-d&amp;c-mediahouse/)</h3><p>A dedicated headless CMS to allow administrators to easily manage, upload, and publish portfolio content.</p><ul><li><strong>Platform:</strong> Sanity Studio (v6.9.x)</li><li><strong>Video Management:</strong> sanity-plugin-mux-input for direct integration with Mux, allowing seamless upload and encoding of high-quality videos straight from the CMS dashboard.</li><li><strong>Content Modeling:</strong> Custom schemas designed specifically for portfolio management (e.g., portfolioProject.ts), enabling structured data entry for projects, categories, and associated media assets.</li></ul><h2>3. Key Features</h2><ul><li><strong>Adaptive Video Streaming (HLS):</strong> All portfolio videos leverage HLS (.m3u8) streaming, ensuring instant playback, dynamic quality adjustment based on user bandwidth, and high performance across devices.</li><li><strong>Optimized Domain Routing:</strong> Utilizes Cloudflare for enterprise-grade, global DNS resolution paired with Vercel's edge caching for maximum frontend delivery speed.</li><li><strong>Cinematic Mode:</strong> An idle-triggered immersive viewing experience that removes UI distractions when the user is focused on video content.</li><li><strong>Dynamic Content Management:</strong> Fully integrated with Sanity CMS, providing the D&amp;C MediaHouse team with real-time content editing capabilities without requiring developer intervention.</li><li><strong>Highly Responsive Design:</strong> Fluidly optimized for mobile, tablet, and desktop viewports utilizing modern Tailwind CSS patterns.</li><li><strong>Automated CI/CD Pipeline:</strong> Seamless updates and zero-downtime deployments via GitHub Actions.</li></ul><h2>4. Development &amp; Setup</h2><h3>Frontend Setup (Next.js)</h3><ol><li>Navigate to the frontend directory: cd dc-mediahouse-next</li><li>Install dependencies: npm install</li><li>Start the development server: npm run dev (Runs on port 3000)</li><li>Build for production: npm run build</li></ol><h3>Legacy Frontend Setup (Vite)</h3><ol><li>Navigate to the frontend directory: cd D&amp;C</li><li>Install dependencies: npm install</li><li>Start the development server: npm run dev</li><li>Build for production: npm run build</li></ol><h3>Sanity Studio Setup</h3><ol><li>Navigate to the studio directory: cd studio-d&amp;c-mediahouse</li><li>Install dependencies: npm install</li><li>Start the Sanity local studio: npm run dev</li><li>Deploy GraphQL APIs: npm run deploy-graphql</li></ol><h2>5. Future Enhancements &amp; Recommendations</h2><ul><li><strong>SEO Optimization:</strong> Ensure dynamic meta-tags, Open Graph (OG) tags, and structured data are generated based on the Sanity content to improve search engine discoverability.</li><li><strong>Analytics:</strong> Integration of web and video analytics (e.g., Mux Data) to track user engagement, video drop-off rates, and overall site performance.</li><li><strong>Asset Optimization:</strong> Continuous monitoring of image payloads from Sanity to ensure they are being served via modern formats (WebP/AVIF) and appropriately sized based on viewport.</li></ul><h2>6. Migration from Vite to Next.js</h2><p>The project frontend was successfully transitioned from a Vite-based Single Page Application (SPA) to Next.js (App Router). The key drivers for this architectural migration were:</p><ul><li><strong>Search Engine Optimization (SEO):</strong> Next.js provides out-of-the-box Server-Side Rendering (SSR), which is critical for a portfolio website to be properly indexed by search engines. The SPA approach with Vite made indexing dynamic meta-tags and content difficult.</li><li><strong>Performance &amp; Core Web Vitals:</strong> Transitioning allowed the use of Next.js built-in optimizations like next/font (eliminating font-related Layout Shifts and flashes of unstyled text) and advanced image optimization, drastically improving initial load times and LCP (Largest Contentful Paint).</li><li><strong>Server Components:</strong> Leveraging React Server Components reduces the JavaScript bundle size delivered to the client, allowing for a snappier, more cinematic user experience.</li><li><strong>Routing &amp; File Structure:</strong> Next.js App Router provides a more robust and scalable file-based routing mechanism compared to client-side routing libraries in Vite.</li></ul>